<title>USA: Ancor Communications names CEO.</title>
<headline>Ancor Communications names CEO.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ancor Communications Inc said Thursday it named Ken Hendrickson as chief executive officer.</p>
<p>Prior to joining Ancor, Hendrickson was executive vice president and general manager for the Microcomputer Products Group at Western Digital Corp where he managed Fibre Channel, a high-speed data communications technology.</p>
<p>Ancor provides high-performance storage and data-intensive network services based on Fibre Channel technology.</p>
<p>Company officials were not immediately available to provide more information.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))  </p>
<p>Hendrickson succeeds Stephen O'Hara, who left the company in April.</p>
<p>The new position will be effective in mid-August.</p>
<p>		((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
